# abssctl

- Package lives under `src/abssctl/`. Version is `__version__` in `src/abssctl/__init__.py`.
- Queue: GitHub Issues. Catch-up: `docs/NEXT_STEPS.md`. Milestone story: `docs/PATH_FORWARD.md`. Workflow: `docs/CURSOR_WORKFLOW.md` and `docs/GITHUB_WORKFLOW.md`.
- Cite `docs/requirements/abssctl-app-specs.txt` and ADRs. Do not paste them into chat.
- One chat per GitHub issue. Hand off with the template in `docs/CURSOR_WORKFLOW.md`.
- Acceptance gate is `make quick-tests`. Docs changes also run `make docs`.
- Do not file an issue or push a tag until a core dev has reviewed the draft in this chat. Capture: `.cursor/skills/capture-todo/SKILL.md`. Release: `.cursor/skills/release/SKILL.md`.
- Actual 25.11+ requires Node >= 22 via `abssctl node ensure`. The CLI installs `@actual-app/sync-server`, not `@actual-app/cli`. npm must be >= 10.9.9. Actual 26.6.0 does not install on an older npm.
- Testing hosts: `docs/TESTING_ACCESS.md`. Only those three VMs. Production server and production PyPI stay untouched.
- Commit only when asked. `ops/session-log.txt` and `ops/ai-directives.txt` are archived.
- Ignore `mutants/` (local mutmut output).
